  "description": "Line-based source text checks and fixes: C# comment reflow, indentation and initializer checks (a faithful port of the briefcases Python formatting scripts, validated by a golden oracle), plus encoding, line endings and whitespace driven by .editorconfig, Razor @code blocks, misplaced warning suppressions, the C# file header (copyright and author lines, attribution lines, copyright year), the C# comment style (two spaces after //, no long dashes, blank lines around the AAA markers, no spec reference), the C# XML doc comments (no doc comment on a test method, the opening of type summaries), the line length against max_line_length and the scenario a [Business (issue, n)] test attribute cites in the design document of its issue; findings can also be written as JUnit and GitLab Code Quality reports, under an explicit exit policy (--fail-on, --tolerate); the severity of an identifier (none, suggestion, warning, error) is set per path with dotnet_diagnostic.<id>.severity in .editorconfig, an identifier is left out per run with --exclude-ids, and the comment wrap width is set with epsitec_comment_line_length. - 1.16.6.2648 net11.0",
